From: Serj Targarien <xergy10@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: adc-joystick - invert an axis by its code, not its index

adc_joystick_invert() looks up the axis's range with input_abs_get_min/max(),
which take an ABS code, but both callers pass the channel index. That only
works where the two happen to match. On the RGB20SX, whose third channel is
ABS_Y, an inverted Y axis read the range of ABS_Z (unset, 0 to 0) and came
out as minus the reading, so the stick rested at about -520: held fully up.

Pass the axis's code.
---
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/adc-joystick.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/adc-joystick.c
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return;
 		if (joy->axes[i].inverted)
-			val = adc_joystick_invert(input, i, val);
+			val = adc_joystick_invert(input, joy->axes[i].code, val);
 		input_report_abs(input, joy->axes[i].code, val);
 	}
 	input_sync(input);
@@ -95,7 +95,7 @@
 		else
 			val &= GENMASK(msb, 0);
 		if (joy->axes[i].inverted)
-			val = adc_joystick_invert(joy->input, i, val);
+			val = adc_joystick_invert(joy->input, joy->axes[i].code, val);
 		input_report_abs(joy->input, joy->axes[i].code, val);
 	}
 
